  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is one of the angles between the normals to the ellipse <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>;&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>cot</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to :"
  },
